{
  "opening": "The marshmallow library is updating its field API to replace deprecated parameter names, which requires marshmallow-jsonschema to align with these changes to maintain compatibility. Specifically, the consumer must adapt to the new naming conventions for default values in marshmallow fields to ensure correct schema generation and avoid deprecation warnings.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "In the marshmallow project, the Field class must accept load_default and dump_default parameters instead of missing and default. The Constant, Nested, and Raw classes must also support these new parameter names while maintaining their existing behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02c",
      "text": "When observed through marshmallow-jsonschema's tests, the marshmallow Field class must correctly handle load_default and dump_default parameters. The Constant, Nested, and Raw classes must similarly support these new parameters without altering their serialization or deserialization logic."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure that all public interfaces are updated accordingly so that marshmallow-jsonschema can function correctly with the new marshmallow release."
}
